**Role:** Comparative case — AI governance framework  
**Claim:** The AI RMF distributes compliance obligations across AI system lifecycle but treats accountability as organisational rather than institutional — it underspecifies answerability to named human authorities.  
**Where used:** §1.4 (AI governance framework literature); §4 (architecture positioned as extension of NIST AI RMF for public administration delegation context)  
**Shared anchor:** [[NIST_AI_RMF]]

