## INSTITUTIONAL CASE SOURCES

### Royal Commission into the Robodebt Scheme (2023)

**Full citation:** Royal Commission into the Robodebt Scheme. (2023). *Report of the Royal Commission into the Robodebt Scheme* (C. Holmes AC SC, Commissioner). Commonwealth of Australia. https://robodebt.royalcommission.gov.au/publications/report  
**Role:** Primary empirical source — Robodebt case  
**Claim:** The Robodebt scheme constituted a systemic failure of institutional answerability in which proxy optimisation (income averaging as a fraud detection mechanism) was implemented without adequate mandate alignment, producing unlawful debt notices at scale.  
**Where used:** §6 (Robodebt case analysis — full institutional reconstruction); §7 (architecture application)  
**Note:** This is the authoritative primary source for Robodebt. All Robodebt case claims must be grounded here.

